---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import DocsSidebar from '../../components/DocsSidebar.astro'
---
<SiteLayout title="AI generation - Open MindMap" description="Connect a host-owned generator to the Open MindMap v0.9 editor with streaming, cancellation, and optional attachments.">
  <div class="shell docs-layout">
    <DocsSidebar active="ai" />

    <article class="docs-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">AI guide</span>
      <h1>Stream structure into the editor.</h1>
      <p>AI generation is an opt-in Editor Feature. The runtime owns parsing, streaming, transaction boundaries, and rollback; your application owns the provider request and credentials.</p>
      <div class="docs-callout">There is no provider key built into the component. Use a server-side proxy or a host <code>request</code> adapter in production, then pass the resulting generator to <code>aiFeature</code>.</div>

      <h2 id="ai-generation">AI generation</h2>
      <p>Install the editor stylesheet and compose the AI Feature with the same <code>MindMapEditor</code> that owns the rest of the editing loop.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; MindMapEditor &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/editor'
import &#123; aiFeature &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/ai'
import '@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/editor.css'
import '@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/features/ai.css'

const ai = aiFeature(&#123;
  generate: async (&#123; prompt, signal &#125;) =&gt; &#123;
    return fetch('/api/mindmap', &#123;
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(&#123; prompt &#125;),
      signal,
    &#125;).then((response) =&gt; response.text())
  &#125;,
&#125;)

const features = [ai]

&lt;MindMapEditor markdown=&#123;markdown&#125; features=&#123;features&#125; /&gt;</code></pre></div>

      <h3>Generator input and result</h3>
      <p>The generator receives the current prompt, serialized Markdown, Document snapshot, an <code>AbortSignal</code>, and any accepted attachments. It can return complete Markdown, an async iterable of delta chunks, or a Promise of either. Keep the AI Feature value stable at module scope or with <code>useMemo</code>; a recreated Feature array can remount its session.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>interface MindMapAIGeneratorInput &#123;
  prompt: string
  markdown: string
  document: MindMapDocument
  signal: AbortSignal
  attachments?: readonly MindMapAIAttachment[]
&#125;

type MindMapAIGeneratorResult =
  | string
  | AsyncIterable&lt;string&gt;
  | Promise&lt;string | AsyncIterable&lt;string&gt;&gt;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Yield deltas rather than cumulative snapshots. The controller coalesces the stream and commits a successful generation as one document transaction.</p>

      <h3>Local or custom generators</h3>
      <p><code>generate</code> and <code>generator</code> are equivalent option names. The browser demo uses a local generator, which keeps prompts and files in the browser.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>async function* localGenerator(&#123; prompt, signal &#125;) &#123;
  const output = `$&#123;prompt&#125;\n- Research\n  - Interview users\n- Delivery`
  for (const chunk of output.match(/.&#123;1,12&#125;/g) ?? []) &#123;
    if (signal.aborted) return
    yield chunk
    await new Promise((resolve) =&gt; setTimeout(resolve, 30))
  &#125;
&#125;

const ai = aiFeature(&#123;
  generate: localGenerator,
  placeholder: 'Describe the map to generate…',
  buttonLabel: 'Generate',
&#125;)</code></pre></div>

      <h3>OpenAI-compatible provider</h3>
      <p>The feature package exports <code>createOpenAICompatibleGenerator</code>. It sends a streaming Chat Completions request and reads text/event-stream responses. The optional <code>request</code> callback lets a host send the payload through its own proxy.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123;
  aiFeature,
  createOpenAICompatibleGenerator,
&#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/ai'

const generate = createOpenAICompatibleGenerator(&#123;
  apiUrl: '/api/mindmap',
  model: 'your-server-model',
&#125;)

const ai = aiFeature(&#123; generate &#125;)</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="config">MindMapAIConfig</h2>
      <p>Use this configuration with <code>createOpenAICompatibleGenerator</code> or pass it as <code>config</code> to <code>aiFeature</code>.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>type AIAttachmentType = 'text' | 'image' | 'pdf'

interface MindMapAIAttachmentLimits &#123;
  maxAttachmentSize?: number
  maxAttachments?: number
  maxTotalAttachmentSize?: number
  attachmentReadConcurrency?: number
&#125;

interface MindMapAIConfig &#123;
  apiUrl: string
  apiKey?: string
  model: string
  systemPrompt?: string
  attachments?: readonly AIAttachmentType[]
  maxAttachmentSize?: number
  maxAttachments?: number
  maxTotalAttachmentSize?: number
  attachmentReadConcurrency?: number
  headers?: Record&lt;string, string&gt;
  request?: (payload: MindMapAIRequestPayload) =&gt; Promise&lt;Response&gt;
&#125;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Feature options take precedence over values nested in <code>config</code>: <code>attachments</code> and each attachment limit can be set at the <code>aiFeature</code> level. With no attachment types (the default), the file picker is hidden. The default reader limits are 5 MiB per file, 10 files, 20 MiB total source bytes, and three concurrent readers.</p>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>apiUrl</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Provider or server proxy endpoint</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>apiKey</code></td><td>No</td><td>Optional bearer credential; keep it server-side when possible</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>model</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Provider model identifier</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>systemPrompt</code></td><td>No</td><td>Replaces the default Markdown mind-map instruction</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>attachments</code></td><td>No</td><td>Allows <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, and/or <code>pdf</code> files; defaults to no file types and hides the picker</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>maxAttachmentSize</code></td><td>No</td><td>Per-file byte limit; defaults to 5 MiB</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>maxAttachments</code></td><td>No</td><td>Total selected file limit; defaults to 10</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>maxTotalAttachmentSize</code></td><td>No</td><td>Total selected source-byte limit; defaults to 20 MiB</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>attachmentReadConcurrency</code></td><td>No</td><td>Concurrent browser readers; defaults to 3</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>headers</code></td><td>No</td><td>Additional request headers</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>request</code></td><td>No</td><td>Host adapter receiving the prepared payload and signal</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h2 id="attachments">Attachments</h2>
      <p>Enable only the attachment types the application needs. The browser reader accepts <code>text/*</code> and <code>.txt</code>, <code>.md</code>, <code>.json</code>, <code>.js</code>, <code>.ts</code>, <code>.xml</code>, <code>.yaml</code>, <code>.yml</code>, <code>.sql</code>, <code>.sh</code>, or <code>.csv</code> files; PNG, JPEG, GIF, or WebP images; and PDF files. It enforces the per-file, total-count, and total-byte limits before reading files.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>const ai = aiFeature(&#123;
  config: &#123;
    apiUrl: '/api/mindmap',
    model: 'your-server-model',
    attachments: ['text', 'image', 'pdf'],
    maxAttachments: 10,
    maxTotalAttachmentSize: 20 * 1024 * 1024,
  &#125;,
  maxAttachmentSize: 2 * 1024 * 1024,
&#125;)</code></pre></div>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Browser input</th><th>Payload part</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>text</code></td><td><code>text/*</code>, <code>.md</code>, <code>.json</code>, <code>.csv</code>, and supported text extensions</td><td>Text content</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>image</code></td><td>PNG, JPEG, GIF, or WebP</td><td><code>image_url</code> with a data URL</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>pdf</code></td><td><code>application/pdf</code></td><td>File part with the data URL; provider support is host-dependent</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p>Attachment validation errors are shown through the localized Feature messages. The optional <code>onError</code> callback receives the original <code>MindMapAttachmentError</code> with code <code>size</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>total-size</code>, <code>type</code>, or <code>read</code>, so a host can log or translate diagnostics without exposing provider details.</p>

      <h2 id="lifecycle">Cancellation, failure, and history</h2>
      <p>While a generation runs, the Feature passes a cancellation signal to the generator. Stopping the request or replacing the controller invalidates the active stream. A successful string replacement or completed delta stream is committed once; cancellation and provider failure leave the previous Document unchanged. The controlled echo guard covers the active transaction and the most recently completed edit or transaction. Use <code>documentRevision</code> and sequence host updates when restoring an older or identical authoritative Document.</p>
      <div class="docs-callout"><code>onDocumentChange</code> and <code>onMarkdownChange</code> are live change notifications and may receive partial stream frames. Persist the latest value when that is the desired policy, and keep the controller as the source of truth instead of maintaining a second tree inside the generator.</div>

      <h2 id="security">Credential and output safety</h2>
      <p>Do not ship long-lived provider credentials in browser JavaScript. A server proxy can authenticate the user, apply rate limits, select the provider, and return only the model output. The runtime parses model output as Markdown; it does not execute code or accept provider HTML as a renderer.</p>
      <p>Use a system prompt that requests a root title and indented list items without a code fence. Validate or constrain provider output at the server boundary when the application needs stricter domain rules.</p>
    </article>

